    <bpmn:process id="W_W1858" name="W1858. Landlord Relationship &amp; Communication Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Ongoing relationship management; maintenance requests; dispute resolution
Frequency: Continuous; ~50–100 landlord interactions/month across portfolio
Volume: ~205 landlord relationships
Owner: Lease Administrator
Participants: Lease Administrator, COO, Store Managers, Legal Counsel
Source: workflow W1858 — Landlord Relationship &amp; Communication Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1858_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1858_Lane1" name="Lease Administrator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1858_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1858_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1858_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1858_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1858_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1858_Lane3" name="Legal Counsel">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1858_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1858_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1858_Start5" name="Ongoing relationship management; maintenance requests; dispute resolution">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1858_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1858_Task6" name="Lease Administrator maintains landlord communication log: (a) all…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Lease Administrator maintains landlord communication log: (a) all correspondence logged in system: date, subject, communication type (email, phone, in-person), participants, (b) open issues tracked with status: pending landlord action, pending BuildRight action, resolved, (c) landlord contact information kept current
Responsible (R): Lease Administrator
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1858_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1858_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1858_Task7" name="Maintenance issue resolution: (a) Store Manager reports maintenance issue to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Maintenance issue resolution: (a) Store Manager reports maintenance issue to Lease Administrator: (i) structural issues (roof leaks, wall cracks, floor damage) — landlord responsibility per most lease agreements, (ii) building systems (electrical supply, water, sewage, fire suppression) — landlord or shared responsibility, (iii) parking lot and exterior maintenance — landlord responsibility, (b) Lease Administrator submits maintenance request to landlord with SLA: urgent (safety/operational impact) — 48 hours; standard — 7 days; (c) if landlord unresponsive: escalate to COO for formal demand letter; Legal Counsel involved if health/safety risk
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Lease Administrator
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Per issue</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1858_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1858_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1858_Task8" name="Quarterly landlord performance review: (a) Lease Administrator compiles…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quarterly landlord performance review: (a) Lease Administrator compiles landlord scorecard: (i) maintenance responsiveness, (ii) building condition, (iii) CAM service quality (cleaning, security, parking), (iv) communication responsiveness, (v) compliance with lease terms, (b) COO reviews underperforming landlords: formal communication requesting improvement; consideration at lease renewal (W1856)
Responsible (R): Lease Administrator / COO
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1858_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1858_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1858_Task9" name="Dispute resolution: (a) if informal resolution fails: Legal Counsel issues…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Dispute resolution: (a) if informal resolution fails: Legal Counsel issues formal demand letter, (b) if landlord disputes maintenance responsibility: Legal Counsel reviews lease agreement and advises, (c) if dispute escalates: mediation per dispute resolution clause in lease; arbitration if mediation fails, (d) COO maintains dispute register with status and resolution timeline
Responsible (R): Legal Counsel / COO
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Per dispute</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1858_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1858_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1858_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1858_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1858_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-367 (ensure controlled execution — Lease Negotiation &amp; Administration (PA-42.1).) | - operational: Lease Administrator review and approval gate
Owner: Lease Administrator</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
