    <bpmn:process id="W_W1860" name="W1860. Sublease &amp; Assignment Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Surplus space available for sublease; assignment to another BuildRight entity
Frequency: ~2–5 sublease arrangements/year
Volume: Typically surplus backroom or office space at store locations
Owner: COO
Participants: COO, Legal Counsel, Finance, Subtenant
Source: workflow W1860 — Sublease &amp; Assignment Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1860_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1860_Lane1" name="COO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1860_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1860_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1860_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1860_Lane2" name="Legal Counsel">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1860_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1860_Lane3" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1860_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1860_Lane4" name="Lease Administrator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1860_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1860_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1860_Start6" name="Surplus space available for sublease; assignment to another BuildRight entity">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1860_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1860_Task7" name="COO identifies surplus space: (a) store backroom larger than needed for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: COO identifies surplus space: (a) store backroom larger than needed for inventory operations, (b) office space above minimum requirement, (c) adjacent space acquired with lease but not needed for retail operations, (d) verify sublease is permitted under master lease (most leases require landlord consent)
Responsible (R): COO
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1860_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1860_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1860_Task8" name="COO obtains landlord consent for sublease: (a) submit sublease request to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: COO obtains landlord consent for sublease: (a) submit sublease request to landlord with proposed subtenant and terms, (b) negotiate landlord&#x27;s consent fee (if any — typically 1 month&#x27;s sublease rent or PHP 50K–100K), (c) confirm landlord retains right to approve/reject subtenant
Responsible (R): COO
Accountable (A): Legal Counsel
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1860_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1860_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1860_Task9" name="Legal Counsel drafts sublease agreement: (a) sublease area, term, rent, and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Legal Counsel drafts sublease agreement: (a) sublease area, term, rent, and conditions, (b) subtenant compliance with master lease terms (no violations that could jeopardize master lease), (c) maintenance responsibilities for subleased area, (d) sublease termination tied to master lease termination, (e) subtenant insurance requirements
Responsible (R): Legal Counsel
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1860_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1860_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1860_Task10" name="Finance processes sublease accounting: (a) record sublease income, (b) PFRS 16…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Finance processes sublease accounting: (a) record sublease income, (b) PFRS 16 treatment: sublease classification (operating vs. finance) based on sublease terms relative to master lease, (c) intercompany sublease (if subtenant is another BuildRight entity): transfer pricing at arm&#x27;s length per W235
Responsible (R): Finance
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Per accounting cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1860_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1860_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1860_Task11" name="Ongoing sublease management: (a) Lease Administrator collects sublease rent…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Ongoing sublease management: (a) Lease Administrator collects sublease rent monthly, (b) monitors subtenant compliance with sublease terms, (c) if subtenant defaults: Legal Counsel initiates sublease termination and eviction per Philippine law
Responsible (R): Lease Administrator
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1860_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1860_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1860_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1860_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1860_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-367 (ensure controlled execution — Lease Negotiation &amp; Administration (PA-42.1).) | - operational: COO review and approval gate
Owner: COO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1860_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1860_Annotation13" targetRef="W1860_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
